# haslerd (runs as pi): clean shutdown from the panel, joining a new Wi-Fi
# from the captive portal (the helper takes SSID/password on stdin, writes
# moOde's network tables, reboots), and the mono switch on the key page (adds
# or removes one ALSA override file), and multiroom (hasler-multiroom: starts
# and stops the snapcast units and points _audioout at the ALSA Loopback in
# /run; it checks its own arguments), and restarting go-librespot after the
# key page renames Spotify Connect (web/room.py; try-restart: only if it runs).
# Accepting a Bluetooth pairing request while the owner's pairing window is
# open (hasler-bt-accept, player/btaccept.py). Remote help, after a press on
# the radio (hasler-help start|status|stop: Tailscale for 24 h, web/help_api.py;
# it checks its own arguments). Restarting MPD when it has stopped answering
# with its process still there (player/watchdog.py MpdRecovery, rate-limited;
# mpd.service's own watchdog drop-in normally gets there first). "Restart the
# radio" on the key page's This radio, after a press on the radio (web/server.py
# restart: systemctl reboot). The time zone, from "Clock and place" on the key
# page (hasler-timezone: it checks its one argument, web/clock.py). Emptying
# the journal when the radio is handed to a new owner (web/handover.py: the
# names of networks, phones and rooms are in it; exactly that one command).
# Nothing else.
# -> /etc/sudoers.d/haslerd (0440, checked with visudo -cf first). Shipped in
# every release as integration/sudoers/haslerd; scripts/install.sh renders it
# for the legacy layout. Updates and yt-dlp go through polkit, not sudo.
pi ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl poweroff, /bin/systemctl poweroff, /usr/bin/systemctl reboot, /bin/systemctl reboot, /usr/local/sbin/hasler-wifi-join, /usr/local/sbin/hasler-audio-mono, /usr/local/sbin/hasler-multiroom, /usr/local/sbin/hasler-bt-accept, /usr/local/sbin/hasler-help, /usr/local/sbin/hasler-timezone, /usr/bin/journalctl --vacuum-time=1s, /usr/bin/systemctl try-restart go-librespot.service, /bin/systemctl try-restart go-librespot.service, /usr/bin/systemctl restart mpd.service, /bin/systemctl restart mpd.service
